---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../../styles/story.css";
import ReadingModes from "../../../components/ReadingModes.astro";
import Cite from "../../../components/Cite.astro";
import SourcedBlock from "../../../components/SourcedBlock.astro";
import StorySources from "../../../components/StorySources.astro";
import StoryState from "../../../components/StoryState.astro";
import StateEvent from "../../../components/StateEvent.astro";
import { readPublishedState, eventPath } from "../../../lib/state.mjs";
import { event, packageEur, doagEur, mffProposedEur, fisheriesAnnualEuro, fisheriesSectoralEur, malmbjergAddedValueEur, satelliteEuEur, satelliteDkDkkMillion, mipUpperSecondary2019, mipUpperSecondary2027, mipRenewable2020, mipRenewable2027, mffProposalDate, ecb, computed } from "../../../data/greenland202609.mjs";
const state = readPublishedState().events.get("event-greenland-september-2026");
if (!state) throw new Error("Missing publication selection: event-greenland-september-2026");
if (state.status === "merged") return Astro.redirect(eventPath(state.survivor), 301);
---
{state.status === "retired" ? <StateEvent view={state} /> : <BaseLayout title={`${event.title} | The Catch`} current="Events">
  <div slot="locator" class="locator"><a href="/events/">Series</a><a href="/events/greenland/">Greenland</a><span>September 2026</span></div>
  <div class="content">
    <main class="story" id="story-root">
      <p class="story-kicker" data-layer="narrative">Nuuk &middot; September 1 to 7, 2026</p>
      <h1 data-layer="fact">{event.title}</h1>
      <p class="story-dek" data-layer="fact">{event.dek}</p>
      <ReadingModes />

      <nav class="story-toc" aria-label="In this story" data-layer="fact">
        <details class="toc-disclosure" open><summary><span>In this story</span><span class="toc-current" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#what-happened">What happened</a></li>
          <li><a href="#the-catch">The catch</a></li>
          <li><a href="#where-this-sits">Where this sits</a></li>
          <li><a href="#who-feels-it">Who feels it</a></li>
          <li><a href="#outlets">What the coverage got right, and what it got wrong</a></li>
          <li><a href="#claim-check">Claim checked against the record</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-happened-next">What happened next</a></li>
          <li><a href="#unknowns">What we do not know yet</a></li>
          <li><a href="#records">The records</a></li>
        </ol>
      </details></nav>
      <div class="kpi-strip" data-layer="fact">
        {event.kpis.map((k) => (
          <div class="kpi">
            <span class="kpi-value">{k.value}<small>{k.unit ? ` ${k.unit}` : ""}</small></span>
            <span class="kpi-label">{k.label}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <aside class="three-things" data-layer="fact">
        <p class="tt-label">Three things to know</p>
        <ol>
          <li>On September 1 the Danish Prime Minister's Office said Jens-Frederik Nielsen, Premier of Greenland (formand for Naalakkersuisut, Greenland's government), would receive European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen and Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen in Nuuk on September 6 and 7 to sign a joint declaration on a stronger EU-Greenland partnership.<Cite s="stm-visit-2026-09-01" passage="01.09.2026" /></li>
          <li>On September 7 the Commission named a €{packageEur} million "Global Gateway Partnership Package" to be invested in and with Greenland this year and the next. Global Gateway is the EU's label for those projects. That figure is in the Commission press release, not in the signed declaration.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="€200 million Global Gateway Partnership Package" /></li>
          <li>The joint declaration signed in Nuuk says it "is not intended to create any legal or financial obligations under domestic or international law."<Cite s="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" passage="This Declaration is not intended to create any legal or financial obligations under domestic or international law" /></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
      <p class="railed rail-note" data-layer="fact">Story updated {event.updated}.</p>

      <div data-layer="proof" class="event-record-context">
        <p class="sources-line">This story rests on the Danish Prime Minister's Office announcement of September 1, the Commission press release, von der Leyen's signing statement, the joint declaration (Commission copy and the Danish government copy), the September 2026 partnership factsheet, Council Decision (EU) 2021/1764, the Commission's Greenland country page, the 2021-2027 programming document, the 2015 joint declaration, the Compilation of Presidential Documents for January 21 and 22, a Truth Social post of January 21, NATO's Arctic Sentry announcement, Danish Defence pages of January 15 and September 1, the European Central Bank's September 8 dollar and krone rates, Nielsen's words as carried by KNR (Greenland's public broadcaster), DR (Denmark's public broadcaster), and the Associated Press, and coverage checked against those records. The Commission's press-corner pages were saved with a browser because the empty shells have no article text. Greenland's own government news listing did not serve the September press release from this machine; KNR quotes that release.</p>
      </div>

      <section id="what-happened">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">September 1 first, then Nuuk</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">What happened</h2>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-visit-2026-09-01" kind="record">
          <p>On September 1, 2026, the Danish Prime Minister's Office said Nielsen would receive von der Leyen and Frederiksen in Nuuk on September 6 and 7. The three leaders were expected to sign a joint declaration on a stronger partnership between the EU and Greenland.<Cite s="stm-visit-2026-09-01" passage="modtager den 6. og 7. september" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-visit-2026-09-01" kind="record">
          <p>Frederiksen said: "Europa har entydigt og uden tøven stået sammen med Grønland og Kongeriget. Stået værn om fundamentale principper som suverænitet og territoriel integritet." In English: Europe has stood with Greenland and the Danish Realm without hesitation, guarding sovereignty and territorial integrity.<Cite s="stm-visit-2026-09-01" passage="Europa har entydigt og uden tøven stået sammen med Grønland og Kongeriget" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="knr-visit-preview-2026-08" kind="record">
          <p>KNR wrote earlier that von der Leyen had been due in Greenland in March, and that the trip was put off after Frederiksen called a Danish Folketing (Danish parliament) election. The same KNR preview said the months of Danish coalition negotiations also added to the wait.<Cite s="knr-visit-preview-2026-08" passage="De månedlange regeringsforhandlinger bidrog ligeledes til ventetiden" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" kind="record">
          <p>On September 1 KNR wrote that Naalakkersuisut had issued a press release. It quoted Nielsen: "EU har meldt klart ud om støtten til os i den geopolitiske situation og samtidig imødekommet vores ønske om et endnu større partnerskab." The EU, he said, had stated its support in the geopolitical situation and had met Greenland's wish for a larger partnership.<Cite s="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" passage="EU har meldt klart ud om støtten til os i den geopolitiske situation" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" kind="record">
          <p>KNR placed the EU visit inside three days of meetings in Nuuk, from 6 to 8 September, that also brought the Faroese premier, Beinir Johannesen, the Realm meeting of Greenland, the Faroe Islands, and Denmark on 7 September, and on 8 September the foreign, security and defence contact committee, with Múte B. Egede and Aqqaluaq B. Egede named among those taking part.<Cite s="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" passage="Fra 6. til 8. september" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dr-ankomst-2026-09-06" kind="record">
          <p>On September 6, DR reported that Frederiksen landed in Nuuk and was greeted by Nielsen, and that von der Leyen's plane landed shortly after. At the arrival press meeting Nielsen said the visit showed "et meget tæt venskab og et godt partnerskab" (a very close friendship and a good partnership). Von der Leyen said: "Vi deler de samme værdier og vi arbejder tæt sammen" (we share the same values and we work closely together).<Cite s="dr-ankomst-2026-09-06" passage="et meget tæt venskab og et godt partnerskab" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>On her visit to Nuuk, von der Leyen announced a €{packageEur} million Global Gateway Partnership Package, "to be invested in and with Greenland this year and the next." That figure is in the Commission press release. The EU, Greenland, and Denmark signed a new Joint Declaration in Nuuk.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="€200 million Global Gateway Partnership Package" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>Von der Leyen said: "Greenland can count on the EU. That was my message during my last visit. Today, I am back to deliver the real results of our close cooperation. With a new EU-Greenland Partnership package, worth €200 million."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="Greenland can count on the EU" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>The Danish government's copy of the declaration is dated 07.09.2026 and ends: "Signed in Nuuk, on 7. september 2026, in three original copies in the English language," for the European Union, the Government of Greenland, and the Government of Denmark.<Cite s="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" passage="Signed in Nuuk, on 7. september 2026" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="statement-26-1803" kind="record">
          <p>In the signing statement von der Leyen named three topics: the Joint Declaration, "the EU-Greenland Partnership Package of EUR 200 million for this year and next year," and "the first deliverables of our partnership package, which are ready to go now."<Cite s="statement-26-1803" passage="EUR 200 million of new investments for Greenland this year and next year" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="statement-26-1803" kind="record">
          <p>The package, she said, focuses on "the big C's: connectivity, clean energy, critical raw materials." A satellite project with Tusass would give northern communities better internet "as of tomorrow," and remote communities in East Greenland "by October."<Cite s="statement-26-1803" passage="connectivity, clean energy, critical raw materials" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="statement-26-1803" kind="record">
          <p>She said the European Union "stands in full solidarity with the Kingdom of Denmark and the people of Greenland," and: "Greenland's future is for the people of Greenland and Denmark to decide, no one else."<Cite s="statement-26-1803" passage="Greenland's future is for the people of Greenland and Denmark to decide, no one else" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Nielsen, speaking at the Nuuk news conference as carried by the Associated Press, called the EU "a loyal and trusted friend" at a time of "new challenges that we cannot tackle alone," and said: "Through these challenging times, your support to us is unfailing. You have stood by us and continue to stand by us. We feel it and are deeply grateful."<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="a loyal and trusted friend" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="av-press-conference-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission's audiovisual service lists a 27-minute "Complete press conference" from Nuuk on 7 September, with opening remarks by Nielsen, von der Leyen, and Frederiksen. That page has no transcript. The words above are AP's text, also carried by CNBC and UPI.<Cite s="av-press-conference-2026-09-07" passage="Complete press conference" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Frederiksen told reporters, as carried by AP: "We have been under pressure. It has been very clear, and we are very thankful for the great support we have received from our European partners but, by the way, also globally."<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="We have been under pressure" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="berlingske-eu-membership-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Berlingske, carrying Ritzau from Nuuk, wrote that Nielsen said EU membership "er ikke på bordet" (is not on the table), and that Greenland still stands where it stood when it left the European Community in 1985.<Cite s="berlingske-eu-membership-2026-09-07" passage="et medlemskab er ikke på bordet" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="euronews-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Euronews quoted Nielsen: "Greenland needs the European Union, and the European Union needs Greenland."<Cite s="euronews-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="Greenland needs the European Union" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>Jozef Síkela, Commissioner for International Partnerships, is quoted on the same Commission release: the partnership is "about creating opportunities that improve people's everyday lives," and "by investing together through Global Gateway, we are strengthening Europe's resilience."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="creating opportunities that improve people's everyday lives" /></p></SourcedBlock>
      </section>

      <section id="the-catch">
        <aside class="the-catch" data-layer="fact">
          <p class="tt-label">The catch</p>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <span class="catch-tag">Told versus record</span>
              <span class="catch-lead">A label, a signature.</span>
              The Commission's press-corner pages for the press release and both statements carry a "Sep 6, 2026 Nuuk" label.<Cite s="statement-26-1804" passage="Statement Sep 6, 2026" /> The Danish government's copy, and the signature block, say the declaration was signed in Nuuk on 7 September 2026.<Cite s="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" passage="Signed in Nuuk, on 7. september 2026" /> DR, writing on September 6 after the planes landed, said "I morgen skal de underskrive" (tomorrow they sign).<Cite s="dr-ankomst-2026-09-06" passage="I morgen skal de underskrive" /> The Commission's digital-policy copy of the same release is labeled "Publication 07 September 2026."<Cite s="digital-strategy-pr-2026-09-07" passage="Publication 07 September 2026" /> The records do not say why the press-corner label and the signature block disagree. <a class="catch-jump" href="#what-happened">What happened</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="catch-tag">Left out</span>
              <span class="catch-lead">On the drawing board.</span>
              KNR, citing Euractiv before the visit, wrote that the EU had an investment package of 150 million euro "på tegnebrættet" (on the drawing board).<Cite s="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" passage="på tegnebrættet" /> The Commission press release that followed is €{packageEur} million.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="€200 million Global Gateway Partnership Package" /> <a class="catch-jump" href="#outlets">Coverage</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="catch-tag">Who pays</span>
              <span class="catch-lead">A total, no split.</span>
              The Commission press release and the partnership factsheet name projects and a €{packageEur} million total.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="€200 million Global Gateway Partnership Package" /> Neither publishes a financing decision, a budget line, or a grant-or-loan split for that sum.<Cite s="eu-greenland-factsheet-2026" passage="Through a new €200 million Global" /> <a class="catch-jump" href="#who-feels-it">Who feels it</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="catch-tag">Told versus record</span>
              <span class="catch-lead">Eleven, or ten plus observers.</span>
              AP wrote that 11 NATO countries began Arctic Shield in Greenland.<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="11 NATO countries" /> Al Jazeera wrote of soldiers from 11 countries of the alliance.<Cite s="aljazeera-greenland-eu-2026-09-08" passage="soldiers from 11 countries of the alliance" /> The Danish Defence page, dated September 1, says "around 400 soldiers, sailors and airmen from 10 NATO nations," and separately lists observer/liaison teams from Poland and Slovenia and an observer team from Germany.<Cite s="forsvaret-arctic-shield-2026" passage="from 10 NATO nations" /> Euronews wrote that soldiers from 10 countries will take part.<Cite s="euronews-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="soldiers from 10 countries" /> Those are two counts with different denominators. <a class="catch-jump" href="#what-happened-next">What happened next</a>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section id="where-this-sits">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The 2015 text, the 2021 envelope, the 2026 record this visit sat inside</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">Where this sits</h2>

        <SourcedBlock source="joint-declaration-2015" kind="record">
          <p>The new declaration says it builds on a Joint Declaration signed in Brussels on 19 March 2015 by the EU, Greenland, and Denmark.<Cite s="joint-declaration-2015" passage="Done at Brussels, on 19 March 2015" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="joint-declaration-2015" kind="record">
          <p>That 2015 text said: "This Declaration is not intended to create any legal or financial obligations under domestic or international law."<Cite s="joint-declaration-2015" passage="This Declaration is not intended to create any legal or financial obligations under domestic or" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="doag-2021-1764" kind="record">
          <p>The legal envelope for the current seven-year budget is Council Decision (EU) 2021/1764 of 5 October 2021, the Decision on the Overseas Association, including Greenland. It allocates "EUR 225 000 000 in the form of grants for bilateral programmable support for the long term development of Greenland."<Cite s="doag-2021-1764" passage="EUR 225 000 000 in the form of grants for bilateral programmable support for the long term development of Greenland" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="mip-2021-greenland" kind="record">
          <p>The 2021-2027 programming document that spends that envelope sets an upper-secondary (high school) completion target of {mipUpperSecondary2027}% by 2027, from {mipUpperSecondary2019}% in 2019, and a renewable share of public energy supply of {mipRenewable2027}% by 2027, from {mipRenewable2020}% in 2020. That is what the €{doagEur} million is for.<Cite s="mip-2021-greenland" passage="2019: 47.9%" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission press release repeats the envelope as €{doagEur} million for 2021-2027, "with 90% dedicated to education and 10% to green growth."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="earmarked €225 million for the period 2021-2027, with 90% dedicated to education and 10% to green growth" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ec-greenland-country" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission's Greenland country page says the proposal to amend the Overseas Association Decision, including €{mffProposedEur} million for Greenland in 2028-2034, was presented on {mffProposalDate}. That date is a year before the Nuuk visit.<Cite s="ec-greenland-country" passage="On 3 September 2025, the European Commission presented a proposal" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission press release restates that proposal as €{mffProposedEur} million "under the next Multiannual Financial Framework 2028-2034, more than doubling the current level of support."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="proposed €530 million for Greenland under the next Multiannual Financial Framework 2028-2034" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="computed">
          <p>{mffProposedEur} divided by {doagEur} is {computed.mffRatio}. That is more than double. The €{packageEur} million package is a separate figure for this year and next, not a rewrite of the €{doagEur} million seven-year envelope.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="proposed €530 million for Greenland under the next Multiannual Financial Framework 2028-2034" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <details class="receipt" data-layer="proof"><summary>how the doubling was counted</summary>
          <p>Commission press release: €530 million proposed for 2028-2034 against €225 million earmarked for 2021-2027. 530 / 225 = {computed.mffRatio}. Education share of the current envelope: 225 × 0.9 = {computed.doagEducationEur} million. Green-growth share: 225 × 0.1 = {computed.doagGreenGrowthEur} million. The proposal date is 3 September 2025 on the Commission Greenland country page, not a Nuuk-week figure.</p>
        </details>

        <SourcedBlock source="forsvaret-greenland-presence-2026-01-15" kind="record">
          <p>On January 15, 2026, Danish Defence said it was raising its activity in and around Greenland with NATO allies, and that from that day it would deploy aircraft, ships, and soldiers, including those from NATO allies. That is the Danish primary for the January presence AP later summarized.<Cite s="forsvaret-greenland-presence-2026-01-15" passage="January 15, 2026" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dcpd-202600046" kind="record">
          <p>On January 21, in remarks at the World Economic Forum in Davos, President Donald Trump said he was asking "to get Greenland, including right, title, and ownership," and: "I don't have to use force. I don't want to use force. I won't use force."<Cite s="dcpd-202600046" passage="right, title, and ownership" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="truthsocial-framework-2026-01-21" kind="record">
          <p>The same day he posted on Truth Social: "we have formed the framework of a future deal with respect to Greenland and, in fact, the entire Arctic Region," and "I will not be imposing the Tariffs that were scheduled to go into effect on February 1st."<Cite s="truthsocial-framework-2026-01-21" passage="framework of a future deal with respect to Greenland" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dcpd-202600051" kind="record">
          <p>On January 22, on Air Force One, he told reporters: "Greenland is going very well. It's in negotiation," and, of a time limit, "The time limit is infinity."<Cite s="dcpd-202600051" passage="The time limit is infinity" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="nato-arctic-sentry-2026-02-11" kind="record">
          <p>On February 11, NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte set out plans for Arctic Sentry, "a new multi-domain activity" to bolster security in the Arctic and High North, initially including Denmark's Arctic Endurance.<Cite s="nato-arctic-sentry-2026-02-11" passage="Arctic Sentry" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>AP later wrote that "Trump eventually backed down after NATO agreed to boost security in the Arctic region." "Backed down" is AP's word.<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="Trump eventually backed down" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-trump-greenland-2026-07-07" kind="record">
          <p>On July 7, in Ankara, Trump told reporters during a meeting with Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan: "That should be controlled by the United States, not by Denmark." We did not find a Compilation of Presidential Documents transcript of that meeting; the sentence here is AP's.<Cite s="ap-trump-greenland-2026-07-07" passage="That should be controlled by the United States, not by Denmark" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="arctictoday-trump-map-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Arctic Today, in its Monday map story, writes that in a July 31 interview on Real America's Voice Trump was asked about a host's prediction that Greenland would be under U.S. operational control before the end of his term, and that the following day he posted an image captioned "Hello, Greenland!" That is Arctic Today's account of those two acts.<Cite s="arctictoday-trump-map-2026-09-07" passage="Hello, Greenland!" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <p data-layer="narrative">Frederiksen's "We have been under pressure" and von der Leyen's "no one else" on September 7 sit on that 2026 record, not on a blank week.<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="We have been under pressure" /></p>

        <SourcedBlock source="dr-signing-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>DR, writing on the signing, put Greenland's mineral weight as its own figure: 24 of the 34 critical raw materials the EU lists can be found in Greenland.<Cite s="dr-signing-2026-09-07" passage="24 af de 34 kritiske råstoffer" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dr-signing-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Jozef Síkela, Commissioner for International Partnerships, told DR the coming Arctic strategy would shift toward peace, security, and economic development while keeping climate and biodiversity as a goal.<Cite s="dr-signing-2026-09-07" passage="fokusere mere på fred og sikkerhed" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="sfpa-greenland" kind="official">
          <p>The Commission's fisheries page puts the current protocol, 12 December 2024 to 11 December 2030, at €{fisheriesAnnualEuro.toLocaleString("en-US")} a year, of which €{fisheriesSectoralEur} million supports Greenland's fisheries policy.<Cite s="sfpa-greenland" passage="€17,296,857 per year" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The September press release rounds that annual total to €17.3 million.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="€17.3 million to Greenland each year under the current fisheries protocol" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>The 2026 declaration recalls that Greenland is an Overseas Country or Territory associated with the EU, and that "the citizens of Greenland, as citizens of the Kingdom of Denmark, have EU citizenship."<Cite s="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" passage="the citizens of Greenland, as citizens of the Kingdom of Denmark, have EU citizenship" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>The 2026 declaration's common objectives include "Resilience, including countering hybrid threats, foreign information manipulation and interference, cooperation on cybersecurity and secure communication."<Cite s="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" passage="countering hybrid threats, foreign information manipulation and interference" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>The 2026 declaration names Part IV of the Treaty on the Functioning of the European Union, the Overseas Association Decision, and the fisheries agreement as "an appropriate framework for the partnership and its continuous development." It also recalls the November 2023 memorandum on raw-material value chains and the 2024 Commission office in Nuuk.<Cite s="stm-joint-declaration-2026-09-07" passage="Council Decision on the Overseas Association, including Greenland" /></p></SourcedBlock>
      </section>

      <section id="who-feels-it">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">Housing, internet, mines, fisheries</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">Who feels it</h2>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission says the package "focuses on investments that improve everyday life in the country: better housing, sustainable tourism and stronger support for small businesses."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="better housing, sustainable tourism and stronger support for small businesses" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission press release says the EU will support the Government of Greenland "through the establishment of a Programme Management Unit," a unit to run the EU-backed programmes.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="through the establishment of a Programme Management Unit" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="statement-26-1803" kind="record">
          <p>Von der Leyen said northern communities would have faster internet "as of tomorrow," and East Greenland remote communities by October, through the Tusass satellite project.<Cite s="statement-26-1803" passage="communities in the Northern part of Greenland" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dr-satellit-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>DR reported that the satellite agreement is expected to give about €{satelliteEuEur} million in EU funds over five years for satellite internet in East and North Greenland, and that Denmark co-finances the project with {satelliteDkDkkMillion} million kroner. Jonas Hasselriis, chief executive of Tusass, Greenland's national tele- og postvirksomhed (telecoms and postal company), said speeds would rise from 6 megabit to 15 megabit, enough to stream as people usually do, and that the extra line matters if the radio chain (the radio relay network along the coast) fails.<Cite s="dr-satellit-2026-09-07" passage="Danmark medfinansierer projektet med 15 millioner kroner" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="eu-greenland-factsheet-2026" kind="record">
          <p>The partnership factsheet names the Tusass Connect subsea cable project as a separate connectivity item from those satellite solutions.<Cite s="eu-greenland-factsheet-2026" passage="Tusass Connect subsea cable project" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission also says it is supporting feasibility work on whether data centres could become viable as energy and digital infrastructure develops, and names Nukissiorfiit, Greenland's national energy utility, for hybrid renewable systems in settlements, and the Buksefjord hydropower plant serving Nuuk.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="whether data centres could become a viable opportunity" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="statement-26-1803" kind="record">
          <p>On mines she named the Malmbjerg molybdenum project, which "could, if we get it right and done, generate up to EUR {malmbjergAddedValueEur} million a year for the country as added value," and GreenRoc's Amitsoq graphite project.<Cite s="statement-26-1803" passage="generate up to EUR 90 million a year" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>The Commission press release calls Amitsoq "an EU Strategic Project under the Critical Raw Materials Act." The factsheet calls the Amitsoq and Malmbjerg projects "concrete examples."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="EU Strategic Project under the Critical Raw Materials Act" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="record">
          <p>Coastal fisheries communities remain on the separate €{fisheriesAnnualEuro.toLocaleString("en-US")}-a-year protocol. The Commission says that money "contributes to economic stability in coastal communities."<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="contributes to economic stability in coastal communities" /></p></SourcedBlock>
      </section>

      <section id="outlets">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The euros, the dollars, the word annexation</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">What the coverage got right, and what it got wrong</h2>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>The Associated Press wrote that von der Leyen offered 200 million euros ($232 million) over the next two years. The €200 million and the two-year window check out against the Commission press release.<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="200 million euros ($232 million)" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ecb-eurofxref-2026-09-08" kind="official">
          <p>The $232 million line is the euro figure at a round dollar rate. The ECB reference rate on September 8 was {ecb.usdPerEur} dollars per euro, which makes €{packageEur} million ${computed.packageUsd} million.<Cite s="ecb-eurofxref-2026-09-08" passage="currency='USD' rate='1.1614'" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>AP also wrote that she wants to "double EU budget support to Greenland to around half a billion euros ($580 million) from 2028." That wording checks out as a round of €{mffProposedEur} million: "around half a billion" is the €500 million neighbourhood of €530 million, and $580 million converts the rounded €500 million. The wording loses €30 million of precision. At the September 8 ECB rate, €{mffProposedEur} million is ${computed.mffProposedUsd} million.<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="around half a billion euros ($580 million)" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <details class="receipt" data-layer="proof"><summary>how those dollars were computed</summary>
          <p>ECB eurofxref daily XML, Cube time 2026-09-08, USD 1.1614, DKK 7.4748. 200 × 1.1614 = 232.28. 530 × 1.1614 = 615.542, shown as 615.54. 200 × 7.4748 = 1494.96. This is a conversion of the Commission figures. It is not a market price for a Greenland security.</p>
        </details>

        <SourcedBlock source="abc-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>ABC News carried the same AP dispatch under the headline "EU chief unveils $232M Greenland package as tensions heighten with Trump claims." The €200 million and the Nielsen and Frederiksen titles check out.<Cite s="abc-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="Trump claims" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="abc-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>The word "claims" is ABC's summary of the January record, including Trump's Davos ask for "right, title, and ownership," not a word in the Nuuk release.<Cite s="dcpd-202600046" passage="right, title, and ownership" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="pbs-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>PBS NewsHour carried the AP text, including "around half a billion euros ($580 million)." The same rounding and conversion as AP: €{mffProposedEur} million is around half a billion, and $580 million converts a rounded €500 million. Exact conversion at the ECB rate is ${computed.mffProposedUsd} million.<Cite s="pbs-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="around half a billion euros ($580 million)" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="cnbc-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>CNBC wrote "200-million-euro ($232.3 million)" and quoted Nielsen and Frederiksen from the news conference. $232.3 million is €200 million at 1.1615 dollars per euro; the ECB rate the next day is 1.1614, which is ${computed.packageUsd} million. That is the same number to one decimal place.<Cite s="cnbc-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="200-million-euro ($232.3 million)" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="upi-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>UPI wrote "$232.3 million" and then referred to Frederiksen as "He said Denmark." Frederiksen is Prime Minister of Denmark. The pronoun is wrong.<Cite s="upi-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="He said Denmark" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="aljazeera-greenland-eu-2026-09-08" kind="checked">
          <p>Al Jazeera wrote "530 million euros ($616m)" for the next budget. 530 × 1.1614 = {computed.mffProposedUsd}, which rounds to $616 million. That conversion checks out.<Cite s="aljazeera-greenland-eu-2026-09-08" passage="530 million euros ($616m)" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="aljazeera-greenland-eu-2026-09-08" kind="checked">
          <p>The word "annex" is Al Jazeera's summary of the January record, not a word in the Nuuk release.<Cite s="dcpd-202600046" passage="right, title, and ownership" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="france24-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>France 24's piece is a preview: datePublished 2026-09-07T00:27Z, which is 22:27 Sunday September 6 in Nuuk, written before the signing. It says von der Leyen "is expected to unveil on Monday a boost in EU investments." There is nothing in that text to check against the Commission press release.<Cite s="france24-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="is expected to unveil on Monday a boost in EU investments" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="reuters-greenland-eu-2026-09-06" kind="checked">
          <p>Reuters wrote that von der Leyen "unveiled plans on Monday for €200 million ($232 million)." The euro figure checks out against the Commission press release. The $232 million line is the same round dollar figure AP used.<Cite s="reuters-greenland-eu-2026-09-06" passage="unveiled plans on Monday for €200 million ($232 million)" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dw-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>Deutsche Welle wrote €200 million ($232 million) and placed the visit after "threats of US annexation earlier this year." The euro figure checks out.<Cite s="dw-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="€200 million ($232 million) investment package" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dw-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="checked">
          <p>"Annexation" is DW's summary of the January record, including the Davos ask for "right, title, and ownership," not a quote from the Nuuk records.<Cite s="dcpd-202600046" passage="right, title, and ownership" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" kind="checked">
          <p>KNR's September 1 story, citing Euractiv, put the package at 150 million euro "på tegnebrættet" (on the drawing board). That is a labeled provisional figure, later superseded by the €200 million Commission press release. We have not saved the Euractiv page.<Cite s="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" passage="på tegnebrættet" /></p></SourcedBlock>
      </section>

      <section id="claim-check">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">"More than doubling"</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">Claim checked against the record</h2>

        <SourcedBlock source="ip-26-1800" kind="computed">
          <p>The Commission says it has proposed €{mffProposedEur} million for Greenland in 2028-2034, "more than doubling the current level of support." The current figure it names in the same paragraph is €{doagEur} million for 2021-2027. {mffProposedEur} / {doagEur} = {computed.mffRatio}. The claim checks out as arithmetic on those two Commission figures. It is a proposal presented on {mffProposalDate}, not money voted in Nuuk.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="more than doubling the current level of support" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <details class="receipt" data-layer="proof"><summary>the two figures in one paragraph</summary>
          <p>Commission press release: "The EU has earmarked €225 million for the period 2021-2027, with 90% dedicated to education and 10% to green growth. The Commission has proposed €530 million for Greenland under the next Multiannual Financial Framework 2028-2034, more than doubling the current level of support." Council Decision (EU) 2021/1764 is the €225 million legal line: "EUR 225 000 000 in the form of grants for bilateral programmable support for the long term development of Greenland." The country page dates the proposal 3 September 2025.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section id="what-happened-next">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The same Monday</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">What happened next</h2>

        <SourcedBlock source="truthsocial-map-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>On Monday, Trump's Truth Social account published a post dated Sep 07, 2026, 10:43 AM. The saved page shows the account name, then the ReTruths and Likes counts, with no accompanying text in between.<Cite s="truthsocial-map-2026-09-07" passage="Sep 07, 2026, 10:43 AM" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="arctictoday-trump-map-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>Arctic Today described that post as a map depicting North America, Central America, the Caribbean, Greenland, and Iceland covered by the U.S. flag and labeled "United States of America," "without accompanying text."<Cite s="arctictoday-trump-map-2026-09-07" passage="without accompanying text" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="thehill-trump-map-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>The Hill described the same Monday post as a map with the American flag over the United States, Canada, Mexico, part of Central America, Greenland, Iceland, and Caribbean islands including Cuba and Jamaica. Separately, The Hill wrote that the White House official account posted on X a Sunday map of New Mexico labeled "New America." That Sunday post is not the Greenland map.<Cite s="thehill-trump-map-2026-09-07" passage="New America" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>AP wrote that von der Leyen's visit came as 11 NATO countries began Arctic Shield exercises in Greenland on Monday, "involving around 400 military personnel," running September 7 to 18, with no U.S. troops taking part.<Cite s="ap-greenland-eu-2026-09-07" passage="Arctic Shield drills, which run Sept. 7-18" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="forsvaret-arctic-shield-2026" kind="record">
          <p>The Danish Defence page, dated September 1, says "around 400 soldiers, sailors and airmen from 10 NATO nations" around Narsarsuaq and Kangerlussuaq from 7 to 18 September, and separately names observer/liaison teams from Poland and Slovenia and an observer team from Germany.<Cite s="forsvaret-arctic-shield-2026" passage="observer/liaison teams from Poland and Slovenia" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="stm-housing-2026-09-08" kind="record">
          <p>The Danish Prime Minister's Office published, dated 07.09.2026, a letter of intent with Naalakkersuisut on Greenland housing. It sets up a joint Greenlandic-Danish working group on publicly owned rental housing, where Naalakkersuisut's national-planning account estimates a maintenance backlog of more than 2.5 billion kroner, and says the working group finishes "inden foråret 2027" (before spring 2027), with concrete projects and financing decided after that.<Cite s="stm-housing-2026-09-08" passage="inden foråret 2027" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="dr-signing-2026-09-07" kind="record">
          <p>DR's September 7 story on the signing recalled that on her 2024 visit von der Leyen was told by then-premier Múte B. Egede that "pæne ord ikke er nok for grønlænderne" (nice words are not enough for Greenlanders) and that concrete investment was needed.<Cite s="dr-signing-2026-09-07" passage="pæne ord ikke er nok for grønlænderne" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <SourcedBlock source="statement-26-1803" kind="record">
          <p>Von der Leyen said the Commission is preparing "a new EU Arctic Strategy to be presented this autumn."<Cite s="statement-26-1803" passage="a new EU Arctic Strategy to be presented this autumn" /></p></SourcedBlock>

        <p data-layer="narrative">Watching: whether the €{packageEur} million is written into a financing decision with dates and a legal basis beyond the press release, and whether the €{mffProposedEur} million survives the 2028-2034 budget talks.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="proposed €530 million for Greenland under the next Multiannual Financial Framework 2028-2034" /></p>
      </section>

      <section id="unknowns">
        <p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">What the records do not hold</p>
        <h2 data-layer="fact">What we do not know yet</h2>

        <p data-layer="narrative">Naalakkersuisut's own September press release is quoted by KNR. The government news listing we saved did not serve that page, so Nielsen's September 1 words here are KNR's quotation of it.<Cite s="knr-topmoede-2026-09-01" passage="Det oplyser naalakkersuisut i en pressemeddelelse" /></p>

        <p data-layer="narrative">The Commission press release names projects and a €{packageEur} million total. It does not publish a table that splits that total by project, year, or budget line.<Cite s="ip-26-1800" passage="€200 million Global Gateway Partnership Package" /></p>

        <p data-layer="narrative">The partnership factsheet also names the total and the projects, without that split.<Cite s="eu-greenland-factsheet-2026" passage="Through a new €200 million Global" /></p>

        <p data-layer="narrative">On the White House briefing-room statements-and-releases page saved September 8, the word Greenland does not appear.<Cite s="wh-statements-releases" passage="September 2, 2026" /></p>

        <p data-layer="narrative">The State Department press-releases listing saved the same day does not name the Commission package.<Cite s="state-press-releases" passage="Press Releases" /></p>
      </section>

